WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:06.520
What is it that I know?

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.940
About this kingdom...

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.950
About war...

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:15.070
About what I must do...

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:24.460
Iskender, where shall we go?

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.470
The Golden Eagle General

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:54.450
Altair: A Record of Battles

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.440
Torqye Stratocracy - Assembly Hall

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.450
"Golden Eagle" Mahmut Pasha

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.490
March, Year 75 of Torqye Rule

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.710
Still studying in the middle of a festival?

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.510
You never change.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:36.670
Ibrahim.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.340
Long time no see, Mahmut.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.680
Heard you finally became Pasha
like you always wanted.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:43.850
Yes.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:48.770
Now should the governor general be using
honorifics with the Pasha in this case?

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:51.060
I don't want you treating me any differently.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:53.520
I thought so.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.820
How is newlywed life?

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.650
Well, actually,

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.570
we just had twins this past summer!

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.740
They're just the cutest things--

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:02.950
Good evening, Ibrahim.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.580
Shara! I can't believe it, it's Shara!

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.700
Mahmut, let me introduce you.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.250
Shara's been at the top of
the best caravansary since we were cadets,

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:15.460
and nowadays she's the number one
dancer in all of Altin!

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.380
I already know who you are.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.430
You came once on your unit's last nights together

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:29.020
before everyone was going to leave
for their new reassignments.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:30.600
You were the soldier

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:33.270
who just sat in the corner
without even dancing,

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.730
looking all serious with your brooding eyes.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.860
Hey, take it easy.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.820
That brooding soldier is now--

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:43.450
I know that too.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:45.200
Tuğril Mahmut Pasha.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.450
I was so surprised.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.370
That soldier from four years ago

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.370
came back as Pasha!

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.830
Let's dance!

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.090
Wait, I--

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.460
Come on!

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.260
I don't like to dance.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:02.510
-Come on!
-Come on!

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.720
Hey, isn't that Mahmut Pasha?

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.390
The Golden Eagle?

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:11.520
That's the youngest person to achieve the rank of Pasha
in the Torqye Stratocracy?

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.190
I heard he passed the military exam when he was 12.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:16.560
He passed that hard test when he was 12?

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.530
Come on!

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.420
I'm happy all your hard work paid off.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:43.260
You were born to become Pasha.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:44.930
What are you looking at?

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.850
People live under these many lights,

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:51.720
each leading their own lives.

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.430
The craftsmen create their goods,

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.440
and the merchants sell them.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:59.070
People are drawn to this city and others like it,

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.940
ultimately shaping our nation of Torqye.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.490
As a Torqye Pasha,

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:06.410
I want to protect these lands.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.910
You're finally able to see your surroundings.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:13.250
Good, good. Maybe you're ready
to show some interest in ladies now?

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.540
What about that Shara?
She's a nice girl!

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.460
What?! I'm not interested in wo--

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:20.840
What's wrong?

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.130
It's gone!

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.800
Did you drop something?

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.470
I can help you look for it.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.300
No, I'll look for it alone.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.150
Welcome home.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:48.450
A Pasha's palace is a lot more modest than I imagined.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.530
It wasn't even locked.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.160
Get out!

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:56.660
What? You don't have to get so mad.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:59.420
"I saw an ocean of stars from the land!

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:03.590
Joyful dancers illuminated underneath the lamps."

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.340
I actually came here to deliver this.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:08.260
Wait!

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.090
Why do you have my book of poems?!

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.300
Here you go.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.140
Did you read all of it?!

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.100
Just where it was bookmarked.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:18.810
I found it in the plaza, and I had a feeling it was yours.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.190
I must have dropped it when you made me dance.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:24.320
Is Mahmut Pasha really going to force
such a kind girl

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:26.320
to walk home alone at night

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:30.490
down these dangerous streets?

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:41.750
Do not come up here under any circumstance.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:45.760
He's so cute! He's still such a kid.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.770
Thief! After him!

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:24.540
It's over. Drop the bag and place your hands
behind your back.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:28.090
Kid, go play policeman somewhere else.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:29.550
I don't have time for this!

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.880
If you comply, I shall leave you unharmed.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:33.550
This is a warning.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:35.430
Warning?

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:38.140
Don't make me laugh!

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:46.570
Thank you, Iskender.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:52.200
Mahmut Pasha!

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.280
An emergency council has been called.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:58.700
Your presence in Altin is required right away.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:00.870
Twelve years ago,

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:05.460
war broke out when the Balt-Rhein Empire
launched a surprise attack against Torqye.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.750
The war ended in a few short months.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:12.760
But relations between the two nations
have been volatile ever since,

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:16.180
as they were locked in
a dangerous balance.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:20.020
On this day, on the western outskirts
of the Torqye border,

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:24.850
the body of Balt-Rhein Empire's Prime Minister Franz
was discovered,

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:30.990
riddled with several arrows
bearing the Torqye crest.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:32.820
The Empire's anger was substantial,

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:35.820
and an arrow stained with
Franz's blood was sent

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.490
along with a letter of denouncement.

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:45.000
It read, "The Empire demands Torqye send one of
your generals to the imperial capital.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:48.670
If there is no reply within seven days,

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:53.720
the Empire shall interpret the assassination of
Prime Minister Franz as a declaration of war.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:55.050
Divan Generals Council

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:56.760
And we will retaliate in kind."

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:00.640
There is no need to give in to such
ridiculous demands. This is war.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:01.930
"Poison" Zaganos Pasha

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:06.400
The Empire has always and will continue to be a threat.
War was inevitable.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:09.730
Absolutely not. The Empire's forces
outnumber ours by tenfold.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:10.900
Şehir Halil Pasha

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:13.740
Torqye has no hope to win.

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:18.200
The Empire would never think
we would initiate the war ourselves.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.410
A surprise attack will give us an advantage.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:25.160
No! Even you must still remember
the war from 12 years ago.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.130
We must avoid repeating that tragedy at all cost.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:33.630
Then Halil Pasha, are you suggesting
we send someone to the Empire as a sacrifice?

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.630
Yes.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.090
Really?

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.640
-Then--
-Please wait!

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:43.640
Are these the only two choices we have to consider?

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:49.650
Is there not a third option that does not lead us to war
or require a sacrifice?

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:53.110
Are the Empire's claims even true
to begin with?

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:56.900
Was it really our soldiers who fired the arrows
at the minister?

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:59.240
I see that you are new.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:03.410
If you are worked up being at your first council,
I suggest calming down.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:06.210
We are currently discussing
whether or not to go to war.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:11.170
I would appreciate it if you didn't criticize the question
simply because you find it too difficult.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:12.340
But--

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:17.130
"I don't want war. I don't want to offer a sacrifice either.
The question is wrong to begin with."

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:19.180
Are you a child?

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:22.560
We do not have the time to be
entertaining the tantrums of a child.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:27.100
I kindly ask any children unable to participate in
thoughtful discussion to excuse themselves.

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:36.490
What's the issue with pointing out
what's wrong?

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:40.990
Are the Pashas only here to choose between
two options?

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:44.410
Of course not! Besides--

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:45.660
Halil Pasha!

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:47.250
Hi!

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:50.920
We haven't had a chance to talk like this in a while.

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:52.460
No, we haven't.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:55.250
I'm sure this is all quite tiring as a new Pasha.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:58.920
No. It's an important meeting to determine
the future of our nation.

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:00.930
I have no time to be tired.

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:02.890
You're a very serious person, Mahmut.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.470
No.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:05.810
Are you upset?

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:07.060
No!

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:09.980
I wouldn't take what Zaganos said to heart.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:12.270
I'm just upset with myself!

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:16.280
Are you thinking about what happened
12 years ago?

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:18.440
Yes.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:22.490
I became Pasha so nothing like that
would ever happen again.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:23.660
But I...

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.030
I haven't done...

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:27.580
What's that?

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:36.920
Then you don't have the time
to be standing still here.

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:42.470
I...

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:43.890
I will never

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:45.890
stand still ever again.

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:50.640
I will do everything that I can.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:55.150
Go on then, Mahmut Pasha.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:59.610
I will also go do what I can.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:04.950
If I could only find evidence that it was not
our soldiers who fired the arrows,

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:07.910
then we would not have to give in to
the Empire's demands.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:19.170
Apparently, our border patrol unit did in fact
witness Imperial forces recover the body,

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:25.510
but that does not prove our forces
had no contact with the minister's party.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.950
These arrow feathers...

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:56.960
In Torqye, our arrow feathers are traditionally
taken from the covert feathers of an eagle.

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:59.550
Yet these arrow feathers

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:02.090
were made from flight feathers.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:05.880
These are traditionally used by the Empire!

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.720
Excuse me, is Halil Pasha here?

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:11.770
I must talk to Halil Pasha!

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:17.100
Mahmut Pasha, Halil Pasha is on his way to the Empire
to take responsibility for the incident.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:20.440
Notification should have been sent already.

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:24.400
Were you the one who made him go?!

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:27.280
Control yourself, Mahmut Pasha.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:30.370
Halil Pasha volunteered himself.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:35.370
Büyük Pasha, I am near retirement.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:38.460
Please allow me to take responsibility
for this incident

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:41.380
and go to the Balt-Rhein Empire.

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:44.760
This nation will survive without me.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:49.350
There are already so many young and talented people
ready to take the reins.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:50.930
No!

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:54.310
This was a plot to incite a war.

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:56.310
He left moments ago.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:59.810
Did Halil Pasha volunteer knowing this?

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:02.070
No! We have to stop him!

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.440
Is this another one of your tantrums?

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:09.410
Then I will accompany him!

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:27.800
So he's come.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:31.800
This is also one of the things I can do, Halil Pasha.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:39.040
I see, a Torqye envoy is on the way.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:42.370
I had guessed they were not ready for war,

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.290
and it seems that I was correct.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.380
Then all we must do is fire the second arrow.

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:48.590
Balt-Rhein Empire Minister Virgilio Louis

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.430
Your Excellence.

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:57.390
We have just received word from our spies
that Torqye has sent an envoy.

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:00.350
Perhaps a patient approach would be best
for the time being.

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:06.150
I am hoping their envoy reaches us
without incident,

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:08.900
but if something unfortunate were to happen...

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:11.530
...we would need your decision.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:17.530
Halil Pasha, there was no reason for you to volunteer.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:21.250
I was Pasha 12 years ago as well.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:22.580
And yet...

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:27.090
I was unable to stop the war.

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:21.770
You must have done everything you could have.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:25.890
You were remarkable, but myself on the other hand...

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:29.150
Mahmut, allow me to say it once again.

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:30.730
I am so sorry.

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:32.610
You have nothing to apologize for!

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:36.070
I was able to come this far because of
everything you did for me!

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.490
But so many people...

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.330
So many children died.

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:44.160
I am willing to do anything to prevent further wars.

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:46.330
This is an Empire conspiracy.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.500
Someone from the Empire killed the minister

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:51.170
and made it seem like Torqye was responsible.

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.420
The Empire planned from the very beginning

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:56.590
to use the minister's assassination
to start a war with Torqye.

00:17:57.220 --> 00:18:00.800
I cannot imagine they will listen to our side
during our delegations.

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:05.020
I volunteered because I thought there was
a chance that they might.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:09.020
Balt-Rhein is the largest nation in Rumeliana.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:13.360
They have the power to start wars
without any political consequences.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:17.700
Yet for some reason they are utilizing
this amount of subterfuge, meaning...

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:21.370
It is not that the Empire as a whole wishes for war.

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:24.620
When we sit down for negotiations,

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:28.710
presenting this evidence you've discovered

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:32.380
will create an opportunity for new dialogue.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:37.170
Your help has drastically raised
the chance of success for our delegation.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:41.260
Your life depends on this arrow feather.

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:45.020
This evidence is not enough to establish
a conspiracy.

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:47.350
If that happens, you will...

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:49.650
No!

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:53.980
There is still something I can do.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:59.700
Okay, do what you think is right.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:03.410
As your first task as Pasha.

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:06.700
Yes, I will protect you, Halil Pasha.

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:08.830
And...

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:12.750
Let us stop this war together!

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:20.340
The Torqye envoy.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:21.640
There it is.

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:36.320
It's empty!

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:37.610
And this is a doll!

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:38.990
What is going on?!

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:41.700
Curses! We have to report back to Minister Louis.

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:43.490
Okay.

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:46.620
So this Minister Louis is the mastermind.

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.370
If I capture you,

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:52.870
I will be able to prove Torqye's innocence.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:55.380
You're going to capture us by yourself?

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:00.550
What is this?!

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:04.550
It's mutton.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:13.520
Go, Iskender!

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:43.970
On this day, the Balt-Rhein Emperor Goldbalt XI

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:47.140
acknowledged the Torqye delegation's testimony
halfway through,

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:50.350
and excused himself before they even finished.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:53.850
This allowed the two nations
to avoid war.

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:56.560
However, this was only the beginning.

00:20:56.730 --> 00:21:03.110
The Empire announced Minister Franz's death
as an unfortunate accident,

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:06.870
and the truth would never come to light.

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:11.580
That concludes our report.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:14.080
Having been saved by Mahmut Pasha,

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:18.590
it seems I will be returning to work
until my retirement.

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:24.590
It had seemed it was all over.

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:30.180
Well done.

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:34.060
But I cannot imagine you will be able
to sustain your luck.

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:37.520
You should refrain from such actions in the future.

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:47.860
However, this was the beginning of the war
that would involve every nation on the continent.

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:51.790
A war that would come to be known as
the Great Rumeliana War.

00:23:27.010 --> 00:23:30.050
Is that true, man of the Empire?

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:32.180
Of course.

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:36.930
This would bring an end to
your hundred years of wandering.

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:40.310
As long as you do as we say,

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:46.400
I promise the fortress city of Hisar will be yours.

00:23:48.860 --> 00:23:50.570
Rebellion in Hisar?

00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:52.700
What's going on, Ibrahim?

00:23:53.160 --> 00:23:55.830
As a friend, I have to help them.

00:23:56.490 --> 00:23:58.240
Next episode, The Citadel City.

00:23:59.120 --> 00:24:01.750
Actor dances in the birdcage.
